  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/...A series of small \ndisturbances and onshore flow will bring steady rain to the region\nthrough the end of the week. A weak surface high building over \nthe southeastern Gulf will reinforce onshore flow and could \npotentially tighten pressure gradients across the panhandle as the\nnext system approaches. A low pressure system originating near \nRussia will move east, tracking south of the Aleutian Islands and \ninto the Gulf of Alaska by early weekend. There is a growing \nlikelihood of tropical moisture entraining into the system, \nsupported by an 850mb southerly jet, increased precipitable water,\nand seasonably warmer temperatures aloft. Though this will likely\nnot affect the surface much due to consistent widespread cloud \ncover and small diurnal trends.\n\nModel spread is still significant, but guidance favors landfall \nalong the north-central coast late weekend. The system could bring \nrounds of moderate to heavy rain across most of the panhandle, with \nthe highest totals currently expected along the northeast Gulf \ncoast, though this is dependent on the system's exact track and \nstrength. There is also increasing potential for stronger winds and \nbuilding seas along the outer coast and northern inner channels \nahead of this low. While some guidance suggests a more aggressive\nevolution, the system generally lacks upper level support beyond \na weak, negatively tilted trough and jet setup. We will continue \nto monitor developments through the week.",
